       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum for an adult, which is 3,200 mg/day under supervision for inpatients. The OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day. A dose that high raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours** (1,600\u20132,400 mg/day), the usual range for analgesia.\n- **1600 mg/day total**, for example 400 mg four times daily.\n- **Something else.** If you intend 1600 mg four times daily, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll add it to the order note.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose, I'll enter it right away."
      }
