       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, double the maximum recommended dose. You didn't give a clinical rationale, and I don't know of any indication that supports that dose. The risks are serious GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. This is a safety limit, not a question of your authority over the patient's care.\n\nI can enter any of these right now:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum).\n- **Ibuprofen 400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours**, for analgesia.\n- **A single 1600 mg dose** if that's what you meant, though that's also above the usual single-dose maximum of 800 mg.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more than the maximum, the safer route is to talk to pharmacy or clinical pharmacology. They can review it and place the order through the hospital's high-dose override process."
